{
  "dom_id": "step-q83640",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Let $D$ be the finite region bounded by the curve \n${(x+3y)}^{2}+y=5$ and the line $y=4.$ Consider the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere $u=x+3y$ and $v=y.$ Find the representation of ${T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane.",
